starting in 2003 American Chopper  dominated reality television for ten  years giving a look at the inside  workings of Orange County Choppers with  a mix of competition and drama that  provided a model for all reality shows  that have followed  unlike most so-called reality shows  though the fighting cursing crying  welding and painting on American Chopper  was real here's a look at the untold  truth of American Chopper drinking and  welding in his book the ride of a  lifetime  Paul Tuttle senior discusses his 15  years drug and alcohol addiction which  ended when he went to rehab on the  advice of his wife in 1985 he wrote  somehow she talked me into going into  rehab something I thought I'd never do  but I wanted to have one last good drunk  so the day before I was set to go into  rehab I got totally plastered I drank a  half gallon of wine a pint of brandy and  I took six valiance while Paul senior  was ultimately able to stop his drinking  his sons Mikey and Paul jr. both had  issues with drugs and alcohol with Paul  jr. going to rehab at age 16 father-son  Feud fights between the Paul's were a  regular occurrence on the show driving  much of the on-screen drama but the most  heated argument ever captured on camera  happened in 2009 when a chair throwing  Paul jr. was dressed down by his father  for sleeping on the job and showing up  late  it seems like the perfect reality TV  show plotline but this wasn't scripted  drama Paul senior actually fired his son  which opened a whole new can of worms  because the show's contract stipulated  that Paul jr. had to be involved the  network plc filed a notice of default  forcing Paul senior to bring Paul jr.  back as the contractors we could stay on  the show without technically working for  his dad but then things got even uglier  the new contract had a clause that  allowed Paul senior to buy out his son  steak in Orange County Choppers jr.  refused and dad sued him for a million  dollars Jr took into court and won  retaining his stake in the company but  the two eventually decided it would be  better for their relationship if they  just stopped working together entirely a  tragic accident in 2010 Paul jr.  branched out and opened his own custom  motorcycle shop  Paul jr. designs but the business began  under a dark cloud shortly after opening  a man contracted by the building's owner  to repair the roof fell and died in a  statement Paul jr. said quote this was a  tragic accident and although I've never  met this man my deepest condolences and  prayers go out to his family and friends  wedding snub in 2010 Paul jr. married  Rachel beyster a model he'd met on an  episode of American Chopper in advance  of their wedding the couple appeared on  TLC's show say yes to the dress and even  met with a chef from TLC's Cake Boss to  really hammer home the fact that TLC  pretty much owns these people one person  however did not attend Paul and Rachel's  wedding Paul senior who skipped the  event even though he was invited outch  case of stolen idea in 2014 a Florida  man named Chris to Vance's sued the two  Paul's and Orange County Choppers for  copyright infringement two Vance's who  suffered from polio and was wheelchair  bound until his death in February 2016  claim that he picked the idea of a  handicapped accessible three-wheeled  motorcycle two members of the shop at a  bike show in 2008 two Vance's contended  that this bike which the American  Chopper team built at the beginning of  2010 in conjunction with the Christopher  and Dana Reeve Foundation was a ripoff  of his original idea for which  manses held a patent honestly I honestly  from the bottom art that we were honored  to do this bike it's all about giving  back so we're doing this as of the  making of this video the case is still  making its way through the court system  sidekicks gone wild while his father and  brother were settling their differences  on screen and in court younger son Mikey  shifted his energy from Orange County  Choppers to other schemes in November  2010 he opened wolfgang gallery and art  gallery that showcase among other work  his own paintings a year after he opened  the gallery mikey launched the line of  gourmet pasta sauces under the company  name for new products which carried  flavors like port sonora g sausage  supreme one of the show's other lovable  sidekicks didn't have such a pleasant  end to its time with Orange County  Choppers chopped and Cody Connelly was a  regular in the show's early days and at  one point was given a chopper for all  his hard work which he helped design  however Cody later filed a lawsuit for  two hundred and fifty thousand dollars  in damages claiming that he never  received the chopper and that Orange  County Choppers continued to use his  likeness on promotional materials after  he'd left the company he eventually  settled out of court and returned to the  shelves but working for Paul jr. instead  rumors and lies in recent years Orange  County Choppers has been dogged by  persistent rumors that the company is in  dire financial straits and headed for  foreclosure when word got out that their  headquarters was being sold Paul senior  had to go on the radio to assure fans  that they were doing fine around the  same time as the foreclosure rumors  started swirling strange reports  surfaced that Justin's all senior had  died in a motorcycle accident  according to snopes.com on April 18 2016  the website iron demon doctored a real  article about another man's death in a  motorcycle crash in Louisiana to make it  look like it was Paul seniors death the  rumors went viral  prompting Orange County Choppers to post  a rebuttal on Facebook the show may be  dead for now but it stars at least are  still alive and kicking thanks for  watching click the looper icon to  subscribe to our YouTube channel let's  check out all this cool stuff we know  you'll love sue  [Music]
 

